      <h1>About slashkern</h1>
      <small>Don’t guess your passion. Test it.</small>
      <h2 id="keep">What we keep</h2>
      <small>As of 9 October 2026</small>
      <table>
        <tr><th scope="row">On your phone</th><td>Your answers, drafts, reflections, your Slash card and settings. Nobody else sees them.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">What leaves your phone</th><td>What you write to Slash, and a prompt you choose to try on the AI, goes to our AI provider (Anthropic) to get a reply; slashkern doesn’t keep it. Things you share yourself. Your account copy, if you make an account (Supabase, EU). Usage counts, only if you say yes.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Delete it</th><td>Settings › Delete my data removes everything on this phone, your Slash card included. Delete my account also removes your account copy, if you have one.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">What a company sees</th><td>Nothing today. Later, only an answer you choose to send for one brand project, never your email. It is off by default, and saying no changes nothing.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">How your card is made</th><td>From your own taps after each project. No AI scores you.</td></tr>
      </table>
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>slashkern is a free app to find your passion by testing different paths. You try short projects in seven fields (design, writing, code, video, selling online, music and prompting with AI), say in 20 seconds how each one felt, and see which path clicks. No account needed.</p>
      <p>Seven creative and digital paths, for now.</p>
      <h2>Who makes it</h2>
      <p>slashkern is made by Manuel Di Paolo, in Italy. Write to <a href="mailto:manuel@trykern.it">manuel@trykern.it</a> for anything: a question, feedback, or your data.</p>
      <h2>For parents</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Age:</b> slashkern is for people aged 18 and over for now, because it is built for adults and keeps what people write. The 18+ check is a tick box for now: we ask, we can’t verify it.</li>
        <li><b>What is stored:</b> without an account, answers, reflections and settings stay in the browser on that device. With an account, a copy is kept at Supabase in the EU (Frankfurt, Germany), so it syncs across devices.</li>
        <li><b>Slash:</b> the AI assistant only asks questions. What someone types to it is sent to the AI provider (Anthropic) to get a reply, and slashkern does not keep it. If a message sounds heavy, it pauses the project and suggests talking to someone they trust or a local helpline.</li>
        <li><b>No ads:</b> no advertising and no cookies. Usage counts stay off unless the person says yes, and never include a name or anything they wrote.</li>
        <li><b>Nothing shared without consent:</b> no company sees an answer unless the person chooses to send it, one project at a time. That is not active yet.</li>
        <li><b>Deleting:</b> in Settings, Delete my data (or Delete my account) removes everything. You can also write to <a href="mailto:manuel@trykern.it">manuel@trykern.it</a>.</li>
      </ul>
